Database migrations (Alembic).

versions/ holds one file per schema change, applied in order (0001, 0002, ...).
env.py reads DATABASE_URL from the environment, else from app.config (which
also loads backend/.env).

From backend/:

    .venv/bin/alembic upgrade head                          # apply everything pending
    .venv/bin/alembic current                               # what this database is at
    .venv/bin/alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what"     # after changing app/models.py

Production: the migrate workflow (.github/workflows/migrate.yml) runs
`alembic upgrade head` against Neon when a change under backend/alembic lands
on main. It needs the DATABASE_URL repository secret.

Guidelines:

- Name files NNNN_short_description.py and set `revision` to the same
  "NNNN_short_description", with down_revision pointing at the previous one.
- Review autogenerated migrations. Autogenerate misses some changes (server
  defaults, renames) and can't write data migrations.
- Keep migrations additive (new tables and columns) where you can. Render
  deploys the same push at the same time, so for a minute the old code may
  run against the new schema, or the new code against the old one.
- Data you can recalculate (stored trade results, cached ESPN payloads) can
  simply be deleted in a migration; the app rebuilds it on the next visit
  (see 0008 and 0009).
